{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/afluent\/backoffjitter"]}],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"BackoffJitter"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","title":"BackoffJitter","platforms":[{"introducedAt":"16.0","name":"iOS","beta":false,"deprecated":false,"unavailable":false},{"introducedAt":"16.0","name":"iPadOS","beta":false,"deprecated":false,"unavailable":false},{"introducedAt":"16.0","name":"Mac Catalyst","beta":false,"deprecated":false,"unavailable":false},{"introducedAt":"13.0","name":"macOS","beta":false,"deprecated":false,"unavailable":false},{"introducedAt":"16.0","name":"tvOS","beta":false,"deprecated":false,"unavailable":false},{"introducedAt":"9.0","name":"watchOS","beta":false,"deprecated":false,"unavailable":false}],"externalID":"s:7Afluent13BackoffJitterV","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"struct","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"BackoffJitter"}],"modules":[{"name":"Afluent"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Afluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Afluent\/RetryStrategies\/BackoffJitter.swift#L31","fileName":"BackoffJitter.swift"}},"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Afluent\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Afluent\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BackoffJitter","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Jitter takes a nominal wait and picks the wait to use instead. It works on any clock’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"Duration","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and the operators that wait take it as a "},{"code":"jitter:","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" parameter:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/ExponentialBackoffStrategy","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" (each backoff delay), "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences\/TimerSequence","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" (where"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each tick falls inside its period) and "},{"code":"delay","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on units of work and sequences (each wait)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The kinds follow “Exponential Backoff and Jitter” (AWS Architecture Blog):"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/BackoffJitter\/none","type":"reference"},{"text":": the nominal wait, exactly.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/BackoffJitter\/full(using:)"},{"type":"text","text":": anywhere from zero up to the nominal wait."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/BackoffJitter\/equal(using:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":": half the nominal wait, plus anywhere up to the other half.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/BackoffJitter\/decorrelated(using:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":": at least the nominal wait, and up to three times the previous wait","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"this jitter produced, so the waits spread further apart the longer they go on.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each random kind draws from the generator it was given, one value per wait, so a seeded"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"generator makes the waits reproducible. A jitter value holds its generator, and for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/BackoffJitter\/decorrelated(using:)"},{"type":"text","text":" the previous wait, by reference: copies of a value share them, and so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"do the operators it is passed to. Make a new value for each operator that should have its own."}]},{"text":"Example","anchor":"Example","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let backoff = ExponentialBackoffStrategy(base: 2, maxDelay: .seconds(60), jitter: .equal())","let heartbeat = TimerSequence.publish(every: .seconds(30), jitter: .full())"],"type":"codeListing"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/BackoffJitter"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How a wait is randomized, so many clients that started waiting together don’t all wake together."}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/BackoffJitter\/none"],"title":"Type Properties","generated":true,"anchor":"Type-Properties"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/BackoffJitter\/decorrelated(using:)","doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/BackoffJitter\/equal(using:)","doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/BackoffJitter\/full(using:)"],"title":"Type Methods","generated":true,"anchor":"Type-Methods"}],"references":{"doc://Afluent/documentation/Afluent/ExponentialBackoffStrategy":{"title":"ExponentialBackoffStrategy","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ExponentialBackoffStrategy","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol"